\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Effect of the \citet  {Roy2016} OLI$\rightarrow $MSI transform over Lake Titicaca water. Native OLI is the Collection-2 surface reflectance recovered by inverting the transform. Reflectance is dimensionless.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:roy}{{1}{13}{}{table.1}{}}
\def\@LN@column{1}
\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Water-specific LS$\rightarrow $S2 recalibration fitted on 270{} paired station--date observations, of the form $\rho _{\mathrm  {S2}} = a + b\,\rho _{\mathrm  {LS,Roy}}$.}}{14}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:localcoef}{{2}{14}{}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.2}The campaign, not the station, is the blocking unit}{14}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:blocking}{{3.2}{14}{}{subsection.3.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Why land-derived harmonization fails over clear water. (a) The Roy intercept relative to the native over-water Landsat signal, by band. (b) Accuracy of a classifier predicting the source sensor from harmonized features; under a successful harmonization it would sit at chance. (c) Sentinel-2 versus harmonized Landsat reflectance on the 270{} paired station--date events; blue agrees worst. (d) Median spectral signature before and after local water recalibration; labels are the Landsat/Sentinel-2 ratio.}}{15}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:harm}{{3}{15}{}{figure.3}{}}
\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Validation design, null models and blocking units (Random Forest, $n=812$ unless noted). A blocking unit is effective only if the corresponding null model collapses under it.}}{16}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:blocking}{{3}{16}{}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Diagnosing the blocking unit. (a) Null models evaluated under campaign-blocked folds: only the campaign-mean null collapses, so only campaign blocking is doing work. (b) Out-of-fold $R^2$ under each validation design and under extrapolation to an unseen trophic zone. That station blocking matches the random split is not evidence of no leakage; it is evidence that station blocking retains nothing.}}{17}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:val}{{4}{17}{}{figure.4}{}}
\citation{Kloiber2002}
