\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Interpretation and operational envelope. (a) Out-of-fold SHAP importance; green and blue dominate. (b) SHAP dependence on the leading feature, by trophic zone. (c) Retrievability of each water-quality variable under the same campaign-blocked design; only transparency clears a useful threshold.}}{26}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:shap}{{7}{26}{}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Transparency trends and their fragility. (a) Annual median in-situ transparency by zone over the full 2011--2024 record, with Mann--Kendall/Sen statistics; no trend is significant. (b) The same test with different start years: beginning the series in 2013, the lowest-median year on record, turns two zones significantly positive.}}{27}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:trends}{{8}{27}{}{figure.8}{}}
